WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.010
<b>Chivalry vs. Fishman Karate</b>

38
00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.220
What's wrong with you, Zoro?

39
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.180
You look like you're having
a really bad day or something.

40
00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.390
I've already demonstrated my way
of the Six Blades to these pathetic humans,

41
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.980
and there's no way you can hope
to defeat me in that condition.

42
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.730
Oh, just shut up already.

43
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.110
Big Bro, he's taken such a beating.

44
00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:16.280
I'm sure the onset of fever caused by his
wounds is making him delirious, or worse.

45
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.950
If that wound opens up again,
I'm afraid he'll die for certain.

46
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.910
But he doesn't have time to
think about that right now.

47
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.920
Yeah, and he's the only one who
can fight that six-sword freak!

48
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.050
I'll show you.

49
00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.130
Three sword style.

50
00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.670
Yosaku!

51
00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:33.550
Johnny!

52
00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.970
Lend me your swords!

53
00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.430
Of course!

54
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:38.720
Big bro!

55
00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:39.550
Catch!

56
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.500
Dammit.

57
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.430
I'm losing it.

58
00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:45.100
I don't know how
much longer I can last.

59
00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.230
Big bro, here they come!

60
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.480
Catch them!

61
00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.110
Now you'll understand why two human
hands never have a chance to beat me!

62
00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.200
Six blades!

63
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.390
Watch out!

64
00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.160
Tentacle Sword Overload!

65
00:02:58.430 --> 00:02:59.530
Big bro!

66
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.500
Three sword style.

67
00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.800
Streaming wolf swords!

68
00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.300
He did it!

69
00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.520
He faced all six swords,
and not even a scratch!

70
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:30.440
Perfect sword skill, with
perfect concentration.

71
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.900
How dare you cut me like that!

72
00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.320
Now I'm really mad!

73
00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.990
I'll kill you, bastard!

74
00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.320
There's no way you'll
survive my next attack!

75
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.620
You just got lucky is all!

76
00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.000
You'll never beat my six
swords with your three!

77
00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.370
I have twice as many swords
as you, don't you get it?

78
00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.540
Six is more!

79
00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.430
I was never very good at math.

80
00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.730
What is it then?

81
00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.840
What weight do you carry
upon your shoulders?

82
00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.050
Three swords.

83
00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.430
Six swords.

84
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.180
Does it matter?

85
00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:12.520
You may have more swords than me, but mine
will always carry more weight than yours!

86
00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.360
He's only been drowned
for a little while.

87
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.580
If we can get him back
up, we can revive him!

88
00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.200
Damn it!

89
00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.590
I can't swing hard enough
underwater to break this thing!

90
00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.000
Hurry, Genzo!

91
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.320
It's no use!

92
00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.340
I can't break it!

93
00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.180
He needs oxygen now, but there's
no time to get an air canister.

94
00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.720
And we can't carry
him up with this rock!

95
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.430
That's it!

96
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.140
Weight, you say?

97
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.980
It may not look like it, but my
swords actually weigh quite a bit.

98
00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.440
Over three hundred
pounds each, to be exact.

99
00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.110
They weigh much more than
your pathetic human swords.

100
00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.120
I meant the burden of... Oh, forget it.

101
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.620
Way of Six Swords!

102
00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:06.830
Octopus pot stance!

103
00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.410
New Year's...

104
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.540
Open!

105
00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:14.960
Body slam!

106
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.120
Cheap shot, stupid octopus!

107
00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.080
How's that?

108
00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.220
Big bro!

109
00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.910
He's dead!

110
00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:24.140
You'll never touch the ground alive!

111
00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.770
Waltz of Six Swords!

112
00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:32.060
You'll be mincemeat if you
touch them for even a second!

113
00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.980
Big bro!

114
00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.440
Yeah!

115
00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.320
Alright!

116
00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.120
Dammit!

117
00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.570
First you timed your roll to dodge
my Tentacle Sword Overload!

118
00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:00.840
Then you slice and dice my hands
up like some cheap Sushi chef!

119
00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.130
How dare you make a spectacle
of my master swordsmanship!

120
00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.520
You'll pay for that, you son of a bitch!

121
00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.430
I'll tear you limb from limb!

122
00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.890
He's in pain.

123
00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.360
That attack, it probably
opened up his wounds again.

124
00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.980
Yeah, I wish I could
take his place right now.

125
00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:26.910
Even if this wound would kill
a normal man, I am not allowed to fail.

126
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.910
Way of Six Swords,
Octopus Pot Stance!

127
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.290
Time to die, Zoro!

128
00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.500
My body cannot feel the pain.

129
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.710
Must not.

130
00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.380
New Year's Open!

131
00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:50.350
If I'm ever going to face Hawkeye as
an equal, I must be extraordinary!

132
00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.900
DRAGON TWISTER!

133
00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.630
Hachi.

134
00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:20.840
Defeated.

135
00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:27.260
Three sword... style.

136
00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:34.140
So, fish.

137
00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.980
Now you finally understand.

138
00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:41.970
The weight I carry in my three swords.

139
00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.900
You satisfied?

140
00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:49.280
Alright.

141
00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.870
Now the tentacles is out of the way.

142
00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:55.330
I think it's time
to go rescue Luffy.

143
00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:56.080
No!

144
00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:56.790
Look out!

145
00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.500
How could you do that to Hachi?

146
00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:01.630
You!

147
00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.150
You thought you'd
gotten rid of me, huh?

148
00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.460
Not bad.

149
00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:10.090
I didn't know there was anyone in all of
the East Blue who could stand back up

150
00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.600
after one of my punches.

151
00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:12.140
Oh, sure.

152
00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:13.850
There's a whole bunch.

153
00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.180
At a certain restaurant I know of.

154
00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:17.060
Wanna go?

155
00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.770
I don't think so.

156
00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.070
Big Bro! Don't do it!

157
00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.940
What do you think you're doing?

158
00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.700
You're dead if you go
in the water like that!

159
00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:29.030
Just shut up.

160
00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.200
It won't last much more.

161
00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.350
You think you ladies might
want to stop chatting?

162
00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:34.330
Yeah.

163
00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:35.160
Time's up.

164
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.460
If I could get you to
shut up for a moment,

165
00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:40.830
maybe you would have noticed
that I was about to do this.

166
00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.840
Here goes nothing!

167
00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.360
That's great!

168
00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.630
He wants to try his luck in the water!

169
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.010
Against a fish man!

170
00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.430
Stupid!

171
00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:57.220
I told you they want us
to fight in the water!

172
00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.910
That man is from Cocoyashi Village!

173
00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.620
They've stretched out Luffy's neck!

174
00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:21.170
Sorry but this is
the best I can do for you.

175
00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:25.290
Please try to breathe. Please come back.

176
00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.630
Damn it, I can't hold my breath much longer.

177
00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.840
You have to come back now.

178
00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:31.800
I see.

179
00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:36.970
They couldn't move the stone so they
just moved Luffy's head above the water.

180
00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:41.690
All I have to do is break the rock apart,
and the situation should take care of itself.

181
00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:49.190
Hahahahaha!
This is more like it.

182
00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.490
Somebody else do something
entertaining! Hahahahaha!

183
00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.200
Ha! It's that old man
from the village...

184
00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.770
What a waste of time.

185
00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:02.040
Dammit! He sees me.

186
00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:03.290
Such a pathetic attempt

187
00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.000
at trying to keep rubber-boy alive!

188
00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.920
Guess I'll just kill you too!

189
00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:13.430
Where do you think you're going?

190
00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:16.930
You... foolish human! Hya!

191
00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.140
Are you really
trying to fight me under water?

192
00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:23.140
You can't even breathe down here.

193
00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.980
What makes you think you can fight?

194
00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.400
As you wish, foolish boy...

195
00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:31.820
Fishman Karate...! Dueling Hair Tether!

196
00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.200
Too bad...

197
00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:42.910
Your kick is powerless down here.

198
00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.380
That's more of your human weakness.

199
00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:49.950
But my Fishman Karate loses
nothing in water. Hahahaha!

200
00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:54.430
Quite the contrary,
it's much more powerful.

201
00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.390
Fishman Karate!

202
00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:01.640
Underwater Bladder Buster!

203
00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.650
Fishman Karate!

204
00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.860
Flaming... Axe Kick!

205
00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:20.990
Back Foot Jawbreaker!

206
00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.500
Guffaw...

207
00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:30.380
... Palm Bomb!

208
00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.880
Air! Air! Air...!
I let out too much!

209
00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.410
I can't breathe... Suffocating...

210
00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.490
Impressive.

211
00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.230
Crap! Let me through.

212
00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:10.130
I need to breathe. Move it!

213
00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.430
You have amazing stamina...

214
00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:13.630
You sure you're human?

215
00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:16.470
Let me through now!

216
00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:23.930
Didn't you say something like, any
man who hurts a lady is just a piece of crap.

217
00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.300
And yet...

218
00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:29.730
Look at what your precious love
of women has gotten you.

219
00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:35.300
You have no escape and
you'll die by my hand.

220
00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.530
The old man and the boy he's
trying to save, they'll die too.

221
00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.980
I'll kill Zoro and the long-nosed guy.

222
00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:44.330
Then I'll massacre the entire village!

223
00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:48.580
And as my final pleasure, I'll
murder that traitorous bitch, Nami!

224
00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.120
Don't you see?

225
00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.460
You're "love" is worthless.

226
00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:56.340
If it can't save you,
then you protect... no one!

227
00:12:56.360 --> 00:13:02.300
Not even your little girlfriend
Nami! Hahahahaha!

228
00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:11.100
I'll admit that you have
some skills... but still...

229
00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:14.610
... in the end you're just a human.

230
00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:20.650
Your body doesn't react well to a
sudden change in pressure, does it?

231
00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:22.910
Let's see...

232
00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:26.200
I have a theory about
what's gonna happen to you...

233
00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:29.790
Your organs are going
to explode from the inside out.

234
00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.540
Pulverizing... Pressure Plunge!

235
00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.180
Hahahaha!

236
00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:47.840
I can't let him do this!

237
00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:52.730
If I want to save Nami, the first
thing I have to do is save myself!

238
00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.160
Huh?

239
00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.450
What's with him?

240
00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.370
He just won't die!

241
00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:15.860
Very well, I guess
we'll just have to try it again!

242
00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:19.200
Fishmen use
lungs to breathe air on land.

243
00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.970
But they use their gills to
breathe water down here,

244
00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:28.470
which means a fish's gills
are useless on dry land.

245
00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.140
Ready for your second go round?

246
00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:36.360
And there lungs
are useless underwater...

247
00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:40.480
... which means forcing air into his
gills should suffocate this bastard.

248
00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:50.410
Hmm?

249
00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.410
You...

250
00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.090
Is he...?

251
00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:00.590
Don't worry. He's okay.

252
00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:01.730
Are you sure?

253
00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:02.700
Half of him.

254
00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:03.720
Wait, half?

255
00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.970
I'll explain later.

256
00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:09.390
First... Get your ass up here...!

257
00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.220
I want to fight where I can breathe.

258
00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.190
You still don't get it, do you?

259
00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:20.520
It doesn't matter to me if
I'm on land or in the water.

260
00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:24.030
I am just as strong either way.

261
00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:27.410
Now you will witness the
true power of Fishman Karate...

262
00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:33.070
When I punched you before, that was
just a sample of things to come.

263
00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:39.420
My ultimate attack, is ten times as powerful
and the chances you'll survive it...

264
00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:42.920
... are zero!

265
00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:44.720
Your neck!

266
00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.800
You said my love was worthless?

267
00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.890
Shoulder!

268
00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:57.160
I can't protect anyone, is that right?

269
00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:03.730
Ribs! Back! Chest! Legs!

270
00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:15.290
Son of a bitch...! Thousand Brick Fist!

271
00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:22.460
And now... Face Shot!

272
00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:45.940
Now it's done... He won't be back.

273
00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.040
Kuroobi...

274
00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.920
Hachi...

275
00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:10.220
In the end
they're all just seafood.

276
00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.340
A fish can't fight a cook.

277
00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:16.010
I don't know what he was thinking.

278
00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.560
This game is ours.

279
00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.560
You bastards...!

280
00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.200
You've killed my brothers
one after the other.

281
00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:31.410
I'm afraid I've let you
get too carried away!

282
00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.620
Alright, explain.

283
00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:37.360
Luffy's half okay...

284
00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.600
What does that mean?

285
00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.800
It means he's alive
for the time being...

286
00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:46.460
but if we want him fully back on dry land,
I've got to go back in the water.

287
00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:51.340
But something tells me
ugly over there won't let me.

288
00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.890
Amazing... really amazing...

289
00:17:56.980 --> 00:18:00.430
Those guys... beat two
of Arlong's best fishmen.

290
00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:07.730
I'm done... I can't hold my breath.

291
00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.490
Take my place. I'll go.

292
00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.330
He spit out a bunch of water.

293
00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:13.560
Did I miss anything?

294
00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.120
They're doing great. Everyone's fine.

295
00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:19.730
For the first time...
I think I have hope...

296
00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:22.040
These guys have fought so well.

297
00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:25.460
We may actually be set free!

298
00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:35.090
Choo. What a pain in the ass!

299
00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:38.510
That long nose freak
sure could run forever.

300
00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:44.690
But it took just one blast from my
squirt gun to take him out completely.

301
00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.690
I guess I should head back.

302
00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:49.940
It's all over by now, for sure.

303
00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.200
It worked! I'm alive!

304
00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:58.290
I am so glad I made the
Ketchup Star for such occasions.

305
00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.830
He thinks he killed me
with a water blast.

306
00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.580
Run along now! Go home!

307
00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:08.380
These guys
are totally freakin' nuts.

308
00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.500
I don't even know what I'm doing here.

309
00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:18.600
They destroyed an entire village
and killed everyone in it.

310
00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:22.640
I know Nami can't do this
all on her own but seriously...

311
00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.690
I'm hearing things.

312
00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:29.770
I don't mind hiding from death.

313
00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.690
Death is scary.

314
00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:35.740
Let's see. I'm covered in fake blood
but I need to look a little more beat up

315
00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:37.660
like I fought bravely.

316
00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.450
Hey I know what's missing.

317
00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.910
Dirt. Yeah, I'm too clean.

318
00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.580
Hey... "I'm sorry, I got lost."

319
00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.750
Yeah, that's good.

320
00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:54.500
No. "I did my best,
but he got me." Maybe.

321
00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:57.490
"I was this close to the
bastard, and he got away."

322
00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:59.330
That sounds better. Nah.

323
00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:01.220
Sounds like I'm trying too hard.

324
00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.920
We're friends...
Right...? So get on.

325
00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:07.020
How 'bout... "Don't cry Nami.

326
00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:09.400
We all did the very best we could."

327
00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.610
Never in my life
did I imagine I'd lose.

328
00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:16.450
Or... "Everybody fought very bravely."

329
00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:19.520
But the truth... is that our
idiot Captain is far better

330
00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.780
than a gang who'd prey on a lady.

331
00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:25.750
Maybe... "I nearly died myself."

332
00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:28.210
It's for my business.

333
00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:30.460
This was my only choice.

334
00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:36.340
"Nami... No, to tell the truth,
my injuries aren't bad at all, really."

335
00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.560
Big Sis Nami was crying.

336
00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:42.350
Do they need any more reason
than that to put their lives on the line?

337
00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:44.960
To make a choice
like that when you're only ten.

338
00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.890
Do you know how hard that
must have been for Nami?

339
00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.810
I fought... bravely...

340
00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:04.160
I never quit... Yeah... that's...

341
00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:09.250
I'm just...

342
00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:11.330
... a liar!

343
00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:20.170
I'm nothing but a coward!

344
00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:23.220
Stop right there, you son of a bitch!

345
00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:28.850
Oh...? You're still alive. Choo.

346
00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.980
That's right, Big Lips...!

347
00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:35.110
It takes more than water
to kill someone like me!

348
00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:35.940
Choo.

349
00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:40.810
When I left
home, I left everything behind.

350
00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:44.240
Peace... Safety...

351
00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:47.740
When you live your life on the edge,
you savor every moment.

352
00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:50.790
That's why they're
able to laugh so much!

353
00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:54.320
That's the reason I went to sea.

354
00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:57.880
I want to laugh that way too.

355
00:21:58.030 --> 00:21:59.830
And if I don't
fight with all I've got,

356
00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:03.890
then I don't deserve to be on
the same ship with them.

357
00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:08.180
And I will never be able
to face my friends again!

358
00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:21.990
Fool... You were better
off pretending to be dead.

359
00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.490
The human brain is
an absolute waste of meat.

360
00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.870
Choo

361
00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:30.540
I... don't feel good.

362
00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:34.620
Oh, yeah...
I'm just getting started.

363
00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.290
Stop it.

364
00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:39.460
Usopp Hammer!

365
00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:42.300
Usopp Rubberband of Doom!

366
00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:47.850
Choo. Arrrgh!

367
00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:52.520
Crap...! Where'd that
stupid son of a bitch go?!

368
00:22:53.030 --> 00:22:56.900
I can't believe this!

369
00:22:57.510 --> 00:22:59.320
Special Attack!

370
00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:00.280
Saké?

371
00:23:00.550 --> 00:23:01.900
Lead Star!

372
00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:07.200
Is this the only way
you can fight, you coward!

373
00:23:07.220 --> 00:23:09.780
There is no place to hide
from my squirt cannon.

374
00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:19.000
Stupid, coward or whatever.

375
00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.800
I can't run from this fight...

376
00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:22.740
I'm supposed to be a man...

377
00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:26.180
Although it doesn't really feel
all that great to be manly.

378
00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:28.470
If I lose, I'll die.

379
00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:30.970
At least I'll die a pirate.

380
00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.430
Squirt Cannon!

381
00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:44.610
Ohhh! No way...! This sucks!

382
00:23:45.210 --> 00:23:46.360
Damn it.

383
00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:49.700
Why should I have to waste
my time with such an idiot?

384
00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:52.080
It's too easy.

385
00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:54.790
I'll shred you to pieces...

386
00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:57.000
Squirt Machine Gun!

387
00:23:58.780 --> 00:24:00.960
How did he find me?

388
00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:02.340
Crap! Crap! Holy Crap!

389
00:24:02.690 --> 00:24:05.590
I wanted to be a real pirate and now
that I've finally gotten my chance.

390
00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:08.050
I know I can do it. I know I can...

391
00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:09.540
I promise...

392
00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:14.100
If I survive this ordeal, I'll never
pretend to be a pirate ever again!

393
00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:16.710
I won't be a coward and run away!

394
00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:20.190
My fake pirate days... are over!

395
00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:24.710
What did you say is done?

396
00:24:24.710 --> 00:24:25.980
This whole fight...

397
00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:27.700
Alcohol lights on fire.

398
00:24:28.080 --> 00:24:30.450
Usopp Flaming Star!

399
00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:35.090
Aaahhh!

400
00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:37.540
Hot, fire, hot, hot!

401
00:24:37.540 --> 00:24:39.030
Water! Must find water!

402
00:24:39.030 --> 00:24:40.030
Water! Water, water!

403
00:24:40.030 --> 00:24:40.870
Wait a minute!

404
00:24:40.870 --> 00:24:43.710
Water, water, water, water!

405
00:24:45.240 --> 00:24:47.130
Usopp Hammer!

406
00:24:47.610 --> 00:24:48.170
Choo!

407
00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:10.780
Bastard!

408
00:25:10.850 --> 00:25:14.660
Usopp Hammer!
Usopp Hammer! Usopp Hammer!

409
00:25:14.660 --> 00:25:15.540
Usopp Hammer!

410
00:25:15.540 --> 00:25:17.160
Rubberband of Doom!

411
00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:18.190
Usopp Hammer! Usopp Hammer!

412
00:25:18.190 --> 00:25:20.790
Usopp Hammer!

413
00:25:30.070 --> 00:25:32.390
I did it! I beat... a fishman...

414
00:25:33.680 --> 00:25:34.720
You see that, loser!

415
00:25:34.740 --> 00:25:36.770
I beat your ass!

416
00:25:41.020 --> 00:25:43.420
I can't believe I actually did it...!

417
00:25:43.420 --> 00:25:47.030
Who's a pirate now...?!
I am Usopp the Pirate!

